WEBVTT

00:00:09.559 --> 00:00:10.749
[RATTLING]

00:00:10.749 --> 00:00:15.819
[BLEEP]

00:00:15.819 --> 00:00:17.229
[HACKING]

00:00:17.229 --> 00:00:18.279
Ah!

00:00:18.279 --> 00:00:20.659
No, no, no, no!

00:00:20.659 --> 00:00:21.709
No!

00:00:21.709 --> 00:00:23.189
[COUGHS]

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.599
[PLOP]

00:00:24.599 --> 00:00:25.649
Huh.

00:00:25.649 --> 00:00:28.419
[MEOWS]

00:00:28.419 --> 00:00:29.469
[CHEERY MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:29.469 --> 00:00:30.519
Um.

00:00:30.519 --> 00:00:32.339
[LIGHT SMACKING]

00:00:32.339 --> 00:00:34.609
Morning, Snowball!

00:00:34.609 --> 00:00:37.629
Who's the best bunny in
the whole wide world?

00:00:37.629 --> 00:00:38.679
[THUMP]

00:00:38.679 --> 00:00:39.729
[BUZZING]

00:00:39.729 --> 00:00:43.539
[HUMMING] eh.

00:00:43.539 --> 00:00:47.929
[SNIFFLING] [GURGLING]

00:00:47.929 --> 00:00:49.529
[CHOMPING]

00:00:49.529 --> 00:00:51.659
Take that, evildoer!

00:00:51.659 --> 00:00:53.519
Off into the sun with you!

00:00:53.519 --> 00:00:54.939
[POW]
- Yeah!

00:00:54.939 --> 00:00:55.989
Shh!

00:01:01.179 --> 00:01:03.179
Ears up.

00:01:03.179 --> 00:01:05.139
[SNAP]

00:01:05.139 --> 00:01:09.059
[ MUSIC - SUPERMAN THEME - JOHN
T. WILLIAMS]

00:01:09.059 --> 00:01:11.019
[LAUGHS] Shwew-shh!

00:01:16.419 --> 00:01:19.219
I'm calling this meeting of
The Superhero Animal Friends

00:01:19.219 --> 00:01:20.379
to order.

00:01:20.379 --> 00:01:22.189
Commander Horsey,
please read the minutes

00:01:22.189 --> 00:01:25.289
from our last meeting.

00:01:25.289 --> 00:01:26.339
Thank you.

00:01:26.339 --> 00:01:28.899
Now, remember everyone,
crime is out there.

00:01:28.899 --> 00:01:30.419
We have to be ready.
MAN: Come on, Molly.

00:01:30.419 --> 00:01:31.469
Time to go.

00:01:31.469 --> 00:01:34.899
Oh, I'm going to
be late for school!

00:01:34.899 --> 00:01:37.319
Captain Snowball, you're
in charge while I'm gone.

00:01:37.319 --> 00:01:39.029
Mu-wah!

00:01:39.029 --> 00:01:40.989
[SLAM]

00:01:40.989 --> 00:01:43.299
First of all, I want
to welcome White Thunder

00:01:43.299 --> 00:01:45.409
back from the washing machine--

00:01:45.409 --> 00:01:47.449
who was put in there
with a red blanket--

00:01:47.449 --> 00:01:52.119
and henceforth, will be
known as Pink Thunder.

00:01:52.119 --> 00:01:54.029
OK, I'm going to
check the perimeter!

00:01:54.029 --> 00:01:56.199
[ MUSIC - SUPERMAN THEME - JOHN
T. WILLIAMS]

00:01:56.199 --> 00:01:57.619
Ha!

00:01:57.619 --> 00:02:02.849
[SNIFFING] [GRUNTING] Good
morning, New York City!

00:02:02.849 --> 00:02:04.839
(SINGING) Da-da, deh duh.

00:02:04.839 --> 00:02:07.329
Da-da, deh duh.

00:02:07.329 --> 00:02:09.319
Da, da, da, de, duh--

00:02:09.319 --> 00:02:10.499
MAX: Snowball?

00:02:10.499 --> 00:02:13.169
Hey, Snowball,
what are you doing?

00:02:13.169 --> 00:02:14.579
What's it look like I'm doing?

00:02:14.579 --> 00:02:16.769
I'm looking for crime, tiny dog!

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:18.259
I'm doing superhero stuff.

00:02:18.259 --> 00:02:19.309
Pit-pit-pit-pit.

00:02:19.309 --> 00:02:21.299
[LAUGHS] Let me
tell you something.

00:02:21.299 --> 00:02:23.639
Anybody comes in here
looking for trouble, oh, they

00:02:23.639 --> 00:02:24.809
gonna meet my partners.

00:02:24.809 --> 00:02:26.859
I'm talking about paw and order.

00:02:26.859 --> 00:02:28.689
[GROWLS] Haw!

00:02:28.689 --> 00:02:30.129
Uh-huh.
OK.

00:02:30.129 --> 00:02:31.929
Well, you do know
that your owner is

00:02:31.929 --> 00:02:33.509
just playing superhero, right?

00:02:33.509 --> 00:02:37.029
[CHUCKLING] You're just
wearing some superhero pajamas.

00:02:37.029 --> 00:02:38.079
Ha!

00:02:38.079 --> 00:02:39.729
Tiny dog, you so naive.

00:02:39.729 --> 00:02:43.279
Point me in the direction of
any animal who needs my help,

00:02:43.279 --> 00:02:44.969
and stand back!

00:02:44.969 --> 00:02:46.359
[MANIACALLY LAUGHS] Whoop!

00:02:46.359 --> 00:02:47.609
[GRUNTING]

00:02:47.609 --> 00:02:49.139
[METAL CLANGS]
Hey, hey, hey!

00:02:49.139 --> 00:02:50.189
Wah!

00:02:50.189 --> 00:02:51.319
[GROWLING]

00:02:51.319 --> 00:02:53.159
OK.
OK.

00:02:53.159 --> 00:02:54.209
I got it.

00:02:54.209 --> 00:02:56.359
So did your kid
leave for school yet?

00:02:56.359 --> 00:02:57.619
Yeah, yeah.
No.

00:02:57.619 --> 00:02:58.849
She's got a quiz today.

00:02:58.849 --> 00:03:01.369
Advanced Spelling,
she'll ace it, though.

00:03:01.369 --> 00:03:03.619
You know, she writes
her answers down in ink.

00:03:03.619 --> 00:03:04.819
That's how confident she is.
[SWISH]

00:03:04.819 --> 00:03:05.869
[THUMP]

00:03:05.869 --> 00:03:07.099
That sounds really smart.

00:03:07.099 --> 00:03:08.149
But you know what?

00:03:08.149 --> 00:03:09.509
Liam is smart too.

00:03:09.509 --> 00:03:13.039
In fact, I heard Katie say
that Liam's head circumference

00:03:13.039 --> 00:03:15.959
is in the 80th percentile.

00:03:15.959 --> 00:03:17.009
Oh, that's cool.

00:03:17.009 --> 00:03:18.059
That's a lot of head.

00:03:18.059 --> 00:03:19.159
Hey, quick question.

00:03:19.159 --> 00:03:20.839
Is he still peeing everywhere?

00:03:20.839 --> 00:03:22.459
Can't control his bladder?

00:03:22.459 --> 00:03:24.589
Yeah, he's--
he's-- he's peeing.

00:03:24.589 --> 00:03:28.129
But-- but every pet knows,
if you pee on it you own it.

00:03:28.129 --> 00:03:30.419
And Liam, he's just
thinking ahead!

00:03:30.419 --> 00:03:31.609
Yeah, but you
still better train

00:03:31.609 --> 00:03:33.049
him before preschool starts.

00:03:33.049 --> 00:03:34.669
You don't want Liam
to get a reputation

00:03:34.669 --> 00:03:35.809
as one of those pee-pee kids.

00:03:35.809 --> 00:03:36.859
Yeah, totally.

00:03:36.859 --> 00:03:37.969
I-- wait.

00:03:37.969 --> 00:03:39.019
Preschool?

00:03:39.019 --> 00:03:40.799
Yeah, he's around that age.

00:03:40.799 --> 00:03:43.249
The baby bird is
leaving the nest, TD.

00:03:43.249 --> 00:03:46.189
No, no, baby bird
is staying put.

00:03:46.189 --> 00:03:48.019
He doesn't need preschool--
he'll you know--

00:03:48.019 --> 00:03:49.069
[SWISHING]
[TAGS CLINKING]

00:03:49.069 --> 00:03:51.649
--stay home with-- [SIGHS]
with me, where it's safe.

00:03:51.649 --> 00:03:54.319
DUKE: Hey, Max,
it's no big deal.

00:03:54.319 --> 00:03:57.929
No need to overreact,
but Liam just left.

00:03:57.929 --> 00:03:59.459
Wait, what?
Where'd he go?

00:03:59.459 --> 00:04:00.509
I don't know.

00:04:00.509 --> 00:04:01.699
They never tell
the dog specifics.

00:04:01.699 --> 00:04:02.749
OK.
OK.

00:04:02.749 --> 00:04:03.799
OK.
[SQUEAKING]

00:04:03.799 --> 00:04:05.329
[THUDDING]
[BEEP]

00:04:05.329 --> 00:04:06.799
This is home base to all units.

00:04:06.799 --> 00:04:08.119
The package has
left the building.

00:04:08.119 --> 00:04:09.289
Does anyone have eyes on him?

00:04:09.289 --> 00:04:10.339
[ENERGETIC MUSIC PLAYING]

00:04:10.339 --> 00:04:13.049
[POP]

00:04:13.049 --> 00:04:14.129
I don't see him.

00:04:14.129 --> 00:04:15.709
Over.
[CRINKLING]

00:04:15.709 --> 00:04:16.759
[CRUNCHING]

00:04:16.759 --> 00:04:17.809
[GULPING]

00:04:17.809 --> 00:04:19.979
Well, he's not in
this bag of chips!

00:04:19.979 --> 00:04:21.309
Over.
- OK.

00:04:21.309 --> 00:04:22.379
Keep-- wait a minute.

00:04:22.379 --> 00:04:23.789
Why would he be
in a bag of chips?

00:04:23.789 --> 00:04:25.379
NORMAN (ON CB RADIO):
Base, this is Eagle Eye.

00:04:25.379 --> 00:04:26.429
Don't you worry.

00:04:26.429 --> 00:04:27.579
[WHIRRING]

00:04:27.579 --> 00:04:28.629
Ah!

00:04:28.629 --> 00:04:30.419
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

00:04:30.419 --> 00:04:33.369
I had eyes on the package as
soon as he left the building.

00:04:33.369 --> 00:04:34.849
Over!
[WHIRRING]

00:04:34.849 --> 00:04:35.899
[CLICK]

00:04:35.899 --> 00:04:38.859
[BEEPING]

00:04:38.859 --> 00:04:40.269
[THUD]

00:04:40.269 --> 00:04:41.319
Uh!

00:04:45.759 --> 00:04:48.369
Subject is safe and sound,
enjoying what looks to be

00:04:48.369 --> 00:04:49.859
a cookie shaped like a moose.
- Here you go.

00:04:49.859 --> 00:04:50.909
[GIGGLING]

00:04:50.909 --> 00:04:52.539
No, wait.

00:04:52.539 --> 00:04:53.949
It's a reindeer!

00:04:53.949 --> 00:04:54.999
OK.

00:04:54.999 --> 00:04:56.099
Thanks, Norman.

00:04:56.099 --> 00:04:57.149
Uh!

00:04:57.149 --> 00:04:58.269
[TAG CLINKING] [GRUNTING]

00:04:58.269 --> 00:05:00.069
Scratching again there, buddy.

00:05:00.069 --> 00:05:01.119
Uh.

00:05:01.119 --> 00:05:02.829
I just-- I really
don't like it when

00:05:02.829 --> 00:05:04.239
they take him out without me.
- Hey, Duke!

00:05:04.239 --> 00:05:05.979
[SQUEAKING]
Moo!

00:05:05.979 --> 00:05:07.749
- [BARKS]
- What's this?

00:05:07.749 --> 00:05:09.459
Oh, I know this!
It's a ball!

00:05:09.459 --> 00:05:10.509
[PANTING]
- Go get it!

00:05:10.509 --> 00:05:11.559
[SLAM]

00:05:11.559 --> 00:05:12.969
DUKE: [BARKING]

00:05:12.969 --> 00:05:15.659
Hey, Maxie, what
say we go for a walk?

00:05:15.659 --> 00:05:17.539
[YIPS] [PANTING] [BEGS]

00:05:17.539 --> 00:05:21.769
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

00:05:21.769 --> 00:05:24.319
You know, I got to
say, this is nice.

00:05:24.319 --> 00:05:26.869
Good to stretch the legs.

00:05:26.869 --> 00:05:30.489
I don't want to go to vet!

00:05:30.489 --> 00:05:32.159
The vet!
No!

00:05:32.159 --> 00:05:33.459
No, no, no, no, no!

00:05:33.459 --> 00:05:36.029
Oh, not cool, you tricked me!

00:05:36.029 --> 00:05:37.549
Maxie, come on boy.

00:05:37.549 --> 00:05:39.959
[WHINING]

00:05:39.959 --> 00:05:41.819
You've been so
stressed lately,

00:05:41.819 --> 00:05:43.529
but this vet is
going to help you.

00:05:43.529 --> 00:05:44.579
Let's go, buddy.

00:05:44.579 --> 00:05:48.499
[YELPING] [CRYING]

00:05:48.499 --> 00:05:49.969
[PANTING]

00:05:49.969 --> 00:05:55.359
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

00:05:55.359 --> 00:05:56.759
Woo.

00:05:56.759 --> 00:05:57.809
Uh.

00:05:57.809 --> 00:05:58.859
[WHINES]

00:05:58.859 --> 00:06:00.419
All right.

00:06:00.419 --> 00:06:01.619
[CRYING]

00:06:01.619 --> 00:06:02.669
Aw.

